Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: expose ThinkSmart amplifier mute GPIO

Use the standard plural GPIO property consumed by the codec driver so it
can control the connected mute line. Preserve the board's existing polarity.

Origin: ThinkSmart View port; see PROVENANCE.md

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -269,8 +269,8 @@
 		reg = <0x49>;
 
 		pdn-gpios = <&tlmm 44 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-		/* The next two GPIOs are connected but unused by the driver */
-		mute-gpio = <&tlmm 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		mute-gpios = <&tlmm 0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		/* Fault indication is not used by the driver. */
 		fault-gpio = <&tlmm 45 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		pvdd-supply = <&speaker_amp_pvdd>;
 
